    },
    {
      "id": "e09",
      "time_offset_ms": 187500,
      "type": "show_result",
      "target": "sql_viewer",
      "params": {},
      "narration": "Three rows, each with a diagnosis. Priya Sharma's diagnosis says inactive but recent order. She's inactive, yes, but her last order date of January fifteenth, twenty twenty-three, is after the cutoff, so deleting her would be a mistake. Fatima Al-Rashid also gets flagged as inactive but recent order. Now, that label isn't quite right for her situation, her last order date is null, not recent, but the key point is the same: we can't confirm she's stale, so she shouldn't be auto-deleted either. Only Amara Johnson earns the truly cleanup target flag. Two out of three would've been wrong deletes.",
      "transition": "continuation",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e09_pause",
      "time_offset_ms": 187950,
      "type": "pause",
      "target": null,
      "params": {
        "duration": 58.0
      },
      "narration": null,
      "transition": "continuation",
      "clears": [],
      "phases": []
    },
    {
      "id": "e10",
      "time_offset_ms": 206833,
      "type": "highlight_section",
      "target": "sql_viewer",
      "params": {
        "section": "fixed_select_before_delete"
      },
      "narration": "Here's the fix. We tighten the WHERE clause so it only catches customers who are inactive and whose last order date is either before the cutoff or null. That way we're deliberate about who we include. Let's SELECT first, because we've learned our lesson.",
      "transition": "new_concept",
      "clears": [
